<title>LATVIA: IBCA SAYS WILL RATE LOCAL BANKS THIS YEAR.</title>
<headline>IBCA SAYS WILL RATE LOCAL BANKS THIS YEAR.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit rating agency IBCA said on Wednesday that it planned to give ratings to a number of Lithuanian banks in 1997.  </p>
<p>&quot;We have spoken to the leading banks in Lithuania...and we will certainly be giving ratings to Lithuanian banks this year,&quot; an IBCA official told Reuters by phone from the company's London office.  </p>
<p>He added that he could not disclose the names of the banks at this time.  </p>
<p>IBCA has yet to assign ratings to banks in the Baltic region.</p>
<p>It gave Lithuania a BB plus long-term foregn currency rating earlier this year.</p>
<p>-- Ed Stoddard, Riga newsroom +371 721 52 40</p>
